# =============================================================================
# The spec forbids committing large binary artifacts. Datasets, tokenized
# corpora, and checkpoints go to Google Drive with links in the README.
#
# NOTE ON THE `!` EXCEPTIONS BELOW
# -------------------------------
# Git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded -- once
# `data/` is ignored, git never descends into it, so `!data/**/whatever` can
# never match. That is why the Phase 1 statistics are COPIED OUT of `data/`
# into `report/phase1/stats/` rather than un-ignored in place, and why the
# tokenizer deliverables live in `<lang>/tokenizer/` (written there by
# `scripts/reselect.py`) rather than only under `data/`.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Corpora and crawl state ------------------------------------------------
data/
*.jsonl
*.jsonl.gz
*.db
*.db-journal

# ---- Tokenized binaries -----------------------------------------------------
*.bin
*.npy
*.idx

# ---- Model checkpoints ------------------------------------------------------
checkpoints/
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt

# ---- Language-ID model (131MB, re-downloadable) -----------------------------
models/lid.176.bin
models/*.partial

# ---- EXCEPTIONS: small Phase 1 deliverables that MUST be committed ----------
# These live outside `data/`, so these negations actually take effect.
!*/tokenizer/*.model
!*/tokenizer/*.vocab
!report/**/*.json
!report/**/*.png
!report/**/*.md
# Phase 2 training logs are .jsonl and live under report/. `*.jsonl` is
# excluded above for corpora, and `!report/**/*.json` does NOT match `.jsonl` --
# so without this line the loss curves, a named Phase 2 deliverable, are
# silently uncommittable.
!report/**/*.jsonl
# Phase 3 synthetic reasoning data. validation/test (~5MB each) are committed
# so graders can read them in the branch; train.jsonl (~28MB) is not -- it is
# regenerated byte-for-byte by `python -m <lang>.reasoning.generate`.
!*/reasoning/dataset/validation.jsonl
!*/reasoning/dataset/test.jsonl
!*/reasoning/dataset/stats.json
!*/reasoning/dataset/samples.md

# ---- Transfer archives ------------------------------------------------------
# Hundreds of MB each; GitHub hard-rejects anything over 100MB, so a single
# `git add -A` without these lines fails the push. Always regenerable from
# make_upload_tars.py.
upload/
*.tar.gz
*.tar
*.zip
_tmp_report/

# =============================================================================
# Working scaffolding — real code, but not Phase 1 deliverables, and in two
# cases actively misleading if committed.
# =============================================================================

# One-off config mutator. The YAML files are the source of truth for every
# threshold; a script that rewrites them in place invites the reader to wonder
# which of the two actually applied. The reasoning it documents is in the
# Phase 1 report §6.1 and §8.
patch_500m.py

# Operational notes written mid-project. Superseded and internally inconsistent
# with the final numbers (it still quotes 479.6M Telugu tokens against the
# measured 674,176,616), so committing it would put two different answers to
# the same question in one repository.
RUNBOOK_500M.md

# Drive transfer tooling and ad-hoc diagnostics. Useful during the run, not
# part of the deliverable set.
make_upload_tars.py
diagnose_manual.py

# Root-level duplicates of <lang>/collect/scrape_news_wave4.py — byte-identical
# copies left over from staging them into the package directories.
telugu_wave4.py
nepali_wave4.py

# Pre-reselect copies of the tokenizer sweep, which record chosen_vocab_size
# 32000 and therefore contradict the 16,000 actually used. The authoritative
# copies are report/phase1/stats/*_tokenizer_sweep.json (chosen 16000,
# sweep_selected_vocab_size 32000).
report/phase1/telugu_tokenizer_sweep.json
report/phase1/nepali_tokenizer_sweep.json

# ---- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/

# ---- OS / editor ------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---- Logs -- but keep any curated log that gets graded ----------------------
*.log
!report/**/*.log

# ---- Staging area for empty/corrupt shards pulled out before a run ----------
data/_empty_shards_to_delete/
